      "publication_year": 2003,
      "publication_date": "2003-01-01",
      "abstract": "In this paper the author reconstructs the meaning of Derrida's concept of \"declarative engagement\". He shows that Derrida revives the modern idea of the \"engaged intellectual\" and even develops it in a radical, prophetic/messianic form. The final consequence of such a position, in the opinion of the author, is a paradoxical coupling of political decisionism with social escapism, which renews in a specific way the nostalgia for the \"heroic role\" of the Marxist intellectual vanguard. This is a major reason for Derrida's popularity in Serbia, it is argued, but can also be taken as the starting point for an analysis of the problem of responsibility of engaged intellectuals.",
